Allow pod cleanup after a host disappears

Provide delete --forget for pods whose SSH host or Kubernetes cluster no
longer exists. Keep --force scoped to bypassing the unmerged-commit
check so transient connection failures do not silently abandon remote
resources.

Use offline listing for forgetting, since even cached listings can query
hosts to warm container IDs. Remove local metadata, connections, and Git
tracking refs without requiring host configuration or backend access.

Cover vanished hosts, unmerged commits, batch deletion, and preservation
of running containers with CLI integration tests.

Disarm pending creation cleanup under the lifecycle lock when
forgetting, so an interrupted launch cannot delete remote resources
afterward. Check cleanup records again after locking to reject stale
directory snapshots. Defer cleanup during startup cancellation as well.
Cover delayed creation and forgetting across daemon restarts.
